             "The owner, 2026-11-12: \"all fences and guards and locks are likely bugs that indicate we have the wrong solution\". What exists (src/seon/ctx.clj, near the end): the agent's record, ```seon.ctx/ctx```, is a plain atom two parties write, the agent by swap! and the system by the patch after each transaction on the branch (on-state, a watch on seon.agent/state). Four props keep the two apart: a validator that does the write (set-validator! calls write!: a side effect in a validator, which Clojure requires to be pure), two dynamic flags (*installing*, no write while the record installs its own value; *writing*, the patch waits until the swap! ends), two module-level volatiles (held, pending) and a watch on ctx that installs the pending value after the swap!. Tests remove and add the watch on seon.agent/state around their bodies (seon.ctx-test lines near 57 and 1370, seon.program-cost-test near 594) for the same reason. The ordinary Clojure way: a type that IS the reference, a deftype implementing clojure.lang.IDeref and clojure.lang.IAtom (as Reagent's RAtom and cursor do): deref answers the record held for the branch's current db; swap! and reset! compute the new value, turn it into one checked transaction (write!'s body), transact it, and the record is the patch of that transaction; the system's patch after any other transaction replaces the held record the same way. One writer path, no validator, no flags, no pending, no watch on ctx. Deletes: the validator, *installing*, *writing*, held's and pending's second roles, the ::written watch, and the tests' watch juggling. Adds no lock, guard or flag. What would show it wrong: a reader that relies on ctx's watches firing on the agent's own swap! (grep add-watch on ctx before building: none on main but ::written), or Context's renders needing the atom's identity. Context owns what an agent sees of ctx: the design goes to it before code; Tests reads the proof. Cost: what write! and patch cost now, no more. Order: after jolt/mergestep and jolt/qualkeys land (Point 0717).",
             :proofs
             [seon.ctx-test/a-swap-and-a-patch-interleaved-give-one-history],
             :instructions
             "Your task: do what the plan below asks, whole. If it names no proofs, write the test that says it is done, reading files if that's what proves it, and register it. You are done when its proofs pass on your branch with main's work merged in. Your status says what stands in the way; once nothing does, your run then ends and root merges your branch."}
