             :plan
             "Found 2026-11-12 (context's loop, a fresh store on jolt/context's worktree): my.agent/grep-leaves-out-the-askers-own-task merged in 18 turns, and its refine (agent l9d0bb167f33a64c) ended :done with 0 model calls. Cause: ```seon.task/refine-decls``` gives a refine the refined task's proofs, green when it ended, and ```seon.task/refine-proofs```, green while the task files load, so ```seon.turn/work!```'s first turn finds ```seon.reconcile/done-explain```'s reasons empty and ends :green before any model call. No refine since 340a97cd66 has read a run. The class: a done rule met before the agent acts; a proof green at the branch's base proves nothing this run did. What a refine's work is (docs/tasks.md#a-refine-curates-its-own-task): a reply naming each change, or saying it found nothing. Plan, settled at the REPL first: a refine's done rule waits on its agent's reply (a reason while its run has made no model call), not on proofs it cannot turn red; weigh against the same reason for every task (a re-run of a green task then costs one call). Loop 2 (2026-11-12) showed the other side: the task capped red, and its refine (m12793c68bbff5ed) capped too, at 40 turns, never editing: a refine changes no code, so the task's red proof can never pass on its branch. Its turns: ~10 finding the run, because the plan says (my.db/at {:branch :task-...}) and the store holds the branch as :main/task-... (seon.db/at looks a branch up by its literal name), and ~20 reading it through seon.ctx.session/session-tx. The branch name is fixed (my.db/at reads a branch as a task names it, seon.repl-test/an-agent-reads-what-its-entities-have-been). The done rule, settled with seon.task/a-step-that-prepares-another-task-is-judged-by-a-proof-over-data (no kinds, no second rule): one rule for every task, AGENTS' red first, in ```seon.reconcile/done-explain```: a run whose proofs were all green at its merge base has proved nothing until its branch changes something (reason :proved-nothing, the content diff both callers already compute); a refine's proofs become refine-proofs alone (the task files load), so it is done once it edits and never waits on the task's red proofs. What to check first at the REPL: which green-at-base runs exist today (a merge step's run, a re-run of a done task) and that each still ends as it should. Proof, red first: a refine of an ended task makes a model call before it ends, and one that changes the task's plan is done though the task's proof is red (scripted provider).",
